# Per-CVE justified skips only -- never a blanket ignore. Add an entry here
# ONLY after confirming (via `trivy image` locally, or a failing ci.yml
# `image` job) that: (1) the CVE has no fix available yet (ci.yml's
# `ignore-unfixed: true` already handles this class automatically -- an
# entry here is for a CVE that DOES have a fix but is accepted anyway, e.g.
# not reachable in this image's actual usage), and (2) the risk is
# genuinely accepted, with a comment explaining why.
#
# As of the last local scan (Firefox ESR 140.14.0esr + geckodriver 0.37.1
# on public.ecr.aws/lambda/python:3.12, Amazon Linux 2023), `trivy image
# --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --vuln-type os,library` found ZERO findings
# across OS packages, Python packages, and the bundled aws-lambda-rie
# binary -- so this file starts empty. Firefox itself pulls a long tail of
# OS-level CVEs over time (design.md's reason for `ignore-unfixed: true`
# in the first place); expect entries to accumulate here as new CVEs are
# published against packages this image can't yet upgrade past.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, `#` comment above explaining the decision.
